  [PASS] 3a AGAINST THE MEASUREMENT HYPOTHESIS -- the sign is not even constant WITHIN a method.  Three of the eight methods contain rows of BOTH signs at |B| > 0.05, and the largest single method group (resolved stellar radial velocities) spans from +1.65 to -0.78.  A calibration offset is one number per method and cannot produce two signs   (methods with both signs: discrete_tracer_RV, resolved_rotation, resolved_star_RV; widest within-method spread resolved_star_RV = 2.431 dex against a TOTAL table spread of 2.805 dex)

    AGAINST THIS PAIR, before it is asserted: the eRASS1 group row's B depends on an assumed stellar +
    gas budget, and h55 itself carries three defensible budgets spanning x1.56 to x2.89 in acceleration
    (B = +0.193 to +0.461).  Taking the budget MOST favourable to the framework, the gap against the
    KiDS keeper shrinks from +0.42 to +0.19 dex.  The pair survives at reduced size, and it survives
    because the KiDS row's own baryonic mass would have to be wrong in the opposite direction by the
    same amount to close it.  The +0.19 dex figure is the one to quote, not the +0.42.
      eRASS1 groups at h55 budget B = +0.193: gap against the KiDS dwarf keeper = +0.189 dex
      eRASS1 groups at h55 budget B = +0.461: gap against the KiDS dwarf keeper = +0.457 dex
  [PASS] 3b THE DECISIVE PAIR, and it is inside ONE method at MATCHED acceleration: the KiDS isolated-dwarf lens stack (lensing, y_bar ~ 1e-3) lands on a_0 and the eRASS1 group lensing masses (lensing, y_bar = 4.2e-3) need +0.42 dex.  Same measurement technique, same decade of acceleration, 0.4 dex apart -- so NEITHER the method NOR the acceleration organises the lensing family   (KiDS dwarf lenses B = +0.004 at y = 1.05e-03; eRASS1 groups B = +0.420 at y = 4.20e-03: +0.416 dex apart on the repo budget and +0.189 on h55's most framework-favourable budget, 0.60 decades apart in y)

